      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ouch, that is sad. Thanks for noticing this.\n\nI think the right way of fixing this is to move the code that triggers the update from EVENT_PROBE_STATUS_CHANGED to EVENT_NETWORK_TESTED. Then we would have only one update for this, and we\u0027d never show the network as validated but with private DNS broken. I think this is safe because NetworkMonitor must always send EVENT_NETWORK_TESTED eventually.\nTo do this well, you will need to add fields for probes attempted and succeeded to NetworkTestedResult, so they can be read in EVENT_NETWORK_TESTED. They are already in NetworkTestedResultParcelable, so you can just read them from there to put them into NetworkTestedResult.\n\nIf we move that code we can also remove handling EVENT_PROBE_STATUS_CHANGED in ConnectivityService, so I think it simplifies things a bit too.\n\nWe already have good test coverage that notifyProbeStatusChanged is called. We\u0027ll want to add some comments in NetworkMonitorTest#testPrivateDnsSuccess. Please review aosp/1817720 :)",
